<title>GERMANY: East-West German wage levels move closer in 1996.</title>
<headline>East-West German wage levels move closer in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The federal Statistics Office on Monday released the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>Average gross monthly wages (in marks unless noted):</p>
<p>					  July 96    July 95    PCT CHG</p>
<p>ALL MANUFACTURING EMPLOYEES</p>
<p> West German			 5,048	 4,954	  +1.9</p>
<p> East German			 3,712	 3,535	  +5.0</p>
<p> East/West ratio (in pct)	 73.5	  71.4	   ---</p>
<p>SALARIED MANUFACTURING EMPLOYEES:</p>
<p> West German			 6,369	 6,183	  +3.0</p>
<p> East German			 4,675	 4,362	  +7.2</p>
<p> East/West ratio (in pct)	 73.4	  70.5	   ---</p>
<p>HOURLY MANUFACTURING EMPLOYEES:</p>
<p> West German			 4,347	 4,337	  +0.2</p>
<p> East German			 3,333	 3,230	  +3.2</p>
<p> East/West ratio (in pct)	 76.7	  74.5	   ---</p>
<p>AVERAGE PAID WORK HOURS PER WEEK IN MANUFACTURING:</p>
<p> West German			  37.9	  38.9	  -2.6</p>
<p> East German			  40.3	  40.2	  +0.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
